wordfreq (word-frequency data)
------------------------------
PresenceAI uses wordfreq (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq), installed as a
separate Python package, to look up English word frequencies. wordfreq's code
is under the Apache License 2.0; its data files are redistributable under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Its data includes:
- Google Books Ngrams (http://books.google.com/ngrams), acknowledged as a source;
- the Leeds Internet Corpus (University of Leeds Centre for Translation Studies),
  Wikipedia and ParaCrawl, under Creative Commons licences;
- OPUS OpenSubtitles 2018 (http://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles.php), from the
  OpenSubtitles project (http://www.opensubtitles.org/);
- SUBTLEX word lists by Marc Brysbaert et al. (SUBTLEX-US, SUBTLEX-UK and others),
  freely available data from http://crr.ugent.be/programs-data/subtitle-frequencies.
Citation: Robyn Speer. (2022). rspeer/wordfreq: v3.0 (v3.0.2). Zenodo.
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7199437
